{
 "fps": 30,
 "total": 18818,
 "xf": 18,
 "titleAfter": 5,
 "shots": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_01.jpg",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 378,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Nineteen seventy-eight. A twenty-year-old pilot is alone over the sea at night. He tells the controller there is a huge shape above him, and that it is not an aircraft.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s01.mp3",
     "dur": 11.52,
     "start": 10,
     "end": 356
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_02.jpg",
   "start": 360,
   "end": 735,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The controller records everything. Then comes seventeen seconds of a strange metallic scraping noise. And then, silence. The pilot and his plane were never found.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s02.mp3",
     "dur": 11.424,
     "start": 370,
     "end": 713
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_03.jpg",
   "start": 717,
   "end": 1019,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Was it a visitor from another world? A pilot lost in the dark? Or something stranger than both? Tonight, we replay the flight recorder.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s03.mp3",
     "dur": 8.976,
     "start": 727,
     "end": 997
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_04.jpg",
   "start": 1001,
   "end": 1271,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "We follow the minutes as they happened. We set the evidence beside each explanation. And at the end, we give a verdict.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s04.mp3",
     "dur": 7.92,
     "start": 1011,
     "end": 1249
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_05.jpg",
   "start": 1253,
   "end": 1612,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The place is Bass Strait, off southern Australia. The date is the twenty-first of October. Let's begin.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s05.mp3",
     "dur": 6.888,
     "start": 1263,
     "end": 1470
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "I \u00b7 THE PILOT",
    "Frederick Valentich",
    "AGE 20 \u00b7 MELBOURNE \u00b7 LICENCE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_06.jpg",
   "start": 1594,
   "end": 1890,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test one. The pilot. Frederick Valentich was twenty years old, from Melbourne. He loved flying, and he wanted to fly for a living.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s06.mp3",
     "dur": 8.784,
     "start": 1604,
     "end": 1868
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_07.jpg",
   "start": 1872,
   "end": 2243,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "He held a private licence, and in May of that year he gained a night rating. He had not yet passed all the exams for a commercial licence. He had failed some of them, twice.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s07.mp3",
     "dur": 11.28,
     "start": 1882,
     "end": 2221
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_08.jpg",
   "start": 2225,
   "end": 2646,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Friends described a careful, keen young man. He was also interested in unidentified flying objects, and had read about them. Investigators later noted that interest in their report.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s08.mp3",
     "dur": 12.96,
     "start": 2235,
     "end": 2624
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_09.jpg",
   "start": 2628,
   "end": 2901,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "This matters, and it cuts both ways. It does not mean he invented a story. But it may have shaped how he read what he saw.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s09.mp3",
     "dur": 8.016,
     "start": 2638,
     "end": 2879
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_10.jpg",
   "start": 2883,
   "end": 3131,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "He was low on night experience, and the sea at night has no horizon. Keep that in mind. It will return.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s10.mp3",
     "dur": 7.2,
     "start": 2893,
     "end": 3109
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_11.jpg",
   "start": 3113,
   "end": 3256,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That evening, he planned a short training flight across the strait.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s11.mp3",
     "dur": 3.696,
     "start": 3123,
     "end": 3234
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "II \u00b7 DEPARTURE",
    "Moorabbin, 18:19",
    "CESSNA 182 \u00b7 FUEL \u00b7 ROUTE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_12.jpg",
   "start": 3238,
   "end": 3531,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test two. The departure. A Cessna one eighty-two, rented from a flying school, filled with fuel for about five hours in the air.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s12.mp3",
     "dur": 8.688,
     "start": 3248,
     "end": 3509
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_13.jpg",
   "start": 3513,
   "end": 3841,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The plan: from Moorabbin airport in Melbourne, to King Island, about two hundred thirty kilometres away. He took off a little after six in the evening.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s13.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 3523,
     "end": 3819
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_14.jpg",
   "start": 3823,
   "end": 4107,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Strangely, he gave different reasons for the trip. Some said he was going to collect friends. Others, that he wanted to buy crayfish.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s14.mp3",
     "dur": 8.376,
     "start": 3833,
     "end": 4085
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_15.jpg",
   "start": 4089,
   "end": 4298,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That is a small thing. But it is the first loose thread, and we will mark it as unverified.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s15.mp3",
     "dur": 5.88,
     "start": 4099,
     "end": 4276
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_16.jpg",
   "start": 4280,
   "end": 4608,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "At seven, he reported over Cape Otway. The weather was good, with excellent visibility and light winds. Daylight would end within twenty minutes.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s16.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 4290,
     "end": 4586
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_17.jpg",
   "start": 4590,
   "end": 4754,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Everything is normal. Now the clock reaches six minutes past seven.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s17.mp3",
     "dur": 4.392,
     "start": 4600,
     "end": 4732
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "III \u00b7 TRANSMISSION",
    "Nineteen Oh Six",
    "THE LAST SIX MINUTES"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_18.jpg",
   "start": 4736,
   "end": 5112,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test three. The transmission. At six minutes past seven, Valentich calls Melbourne flight service. He asks if there is any known traffic below five thousand feet.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s18.mp3",
     "dur": 11.448,
     "start": 4746,
     "end": 5090
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_19.jpg",
   "start": 5094,
   "end": 5274,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The controller checks. There is no known traffic. Nothing is expected near him.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s19.mp3",
     "dur": 4.92,
     "start": 5104,
     "end": 5252
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_20.jpg",
   "start": 5256,
   "end": 5588,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Valentich says a large aircraft is there, with four bright lights that look like landing lights. It has passed over him, about a thousand feet above.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s20.mp3",
     "dur": 9.984,
     "start": 5266,
     "end": 5566
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_21.jpg",
   "start": 5570,
   "end": 5925,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "He says it is moving at high speed, and it seems to be playing with him. He guesses it could be going one hundred miles an hour, then tries again to describe it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s21.mp3",
     "dur": 10.752,
     "start": 5580,
     "end": 5903
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_22.jpg",
   "start": 5907,
   "end": 6226,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The controller asks him to identify the aircraft type. Valentich says he cannot. It is a long shape, he says, shiny, and metallic-looking.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s22.mp3",
     "dur": 9.552,
     "start": 5917,
     "end": 6204
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_23.jpg",
   "start": 6208,
   "end": 6517,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then he reports a green light, and something like a mist, and a pulsing, as it comes closer. This is the detail that puzzles pilots most.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s23.mp3",
     "dur": 9.216,
     "start": 6218,
     "end": 6495
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_24.jpg",
   "start": 6499,
   "end": 6809,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Then, his engine begins to run rough. He is flying at about four thousand five hundred feet, and he reports the strange craft overhead.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s24.mp3",
     "dur": 9.264,
     "start": 6509,
     "end": 6787
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_25.jpg",
   "start": 6791,
   "end": 7091,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "He says it is hovering, and that it is not an aircraft. Those words are among the most famous in the history of unexplained sightings.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s25.mp3",
     "dur": 8.904,
     "start": 6801,
     "end": 7069
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_26.jpg",
   "start": 7073,
   "end": 7401,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The controller replies calmly, asking his intentions. Valentich says he plans to carry on to King Island, and that the object is above him again.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s26.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 7083,
     "end": 7379
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_27.jpg",
   "start": 7383,
   "end": 7650,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "His last intelligible words are something like: it is not an aircraft, it is. And then the microphone stays open.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s27.mp3",
     "dur": 7.824,
     "start": 7393,
     "end": 7628
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_28.jpg",
   "start": 7632,
   "end": 7965,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "For seventeen seconds, the tape records a harsh metallic scraping sound. Then nothing. That is the last evidence we have of Frederick Valentich.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s28.mp3",
     "dur": 10.008,
     "start": 7642,
     "end": 7943
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_29.jpg",
   "start": 7947,
   "end": 8253,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The controller calls him again. There is no answer. Within minutes, the alert phase begins, and at half past seven, a full distress phase.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s29.mp3",
     "dur": 9.12,
     "start": 7957,
     "end": 8231
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_30.jpg",
   "start": 8235,
   "end": 8494,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Search aircraft take off through the night and the following days, including an air force Orion and civilian planes.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s30.mp3",
     "dur": 7.536,
     "start": 8245,
     "end": 8472
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_31.jpg",
   "start": 8476,
   "end": 8623,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test three complete. A voice, a sound, and an empty sea.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s31.mp3",
     "dur": 3.816,
     "start": 8486,
     "end": 8601
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "IV \u00b7 THE SEARCH",
    "Four Days, Nothing",
    "2,600 KM\u00b2 \u00b7 ORION \u00b7 NO WRECKAGE"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_32.jpg",
   "start": 8605,
   "end": 8890,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test four. The search. For four days, aircraft and ships cover more than two thousand six hundred square kilometres of Bass Strait.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s32.mp3",
     "dur": 8.424,
     "start": 8615,
     "end": 8868
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_33.jpg",
   "start": 8872,
   "end": 9086,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "They find no wreckage. No oil slick that can be linked to him. No life raft. No body.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s33.mp3",
     "dur": 6.048,
     "start": 8882,
     "end": 9064
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_34.jpg",
   "start": 9068,
   "end": 9387,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That is odd, but not impossible. Cold, deep water and strong currents can swallow a small aircraft, and the strait is known for its storms.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s34.mp3",
     "dur": 9.552,
     "start": 9078,
     "end": 9365
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_35.jpg",
   "start": 9369,
   "end": 9754,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "In nineteen eighty-three, a piece of engine cowling washes ashore on Flinders Island. It might be from a Cessna one eighty-two. It was never proven to be from his plane.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s35.mp3",
     "dur": 11.76,
     "start": 9379,
     "end": 9732
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_36.jpg",
   "start": 9736,
   "end": 9995,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A naval laboratory said drift from the crash area was plausible. But a possible fragment is not a confirmed one.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s36.mp3",
     "dur": 7.536,
     "start": 9746,
     "end": 9973
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_37.jpg",
   "start": 9977,
   "end": 10172,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The sea kept its secret. So the official investigators had to decide what to write.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s37.mp3",
     "dur": 5.424,
     "start": 9987,
     "end": 10150
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": [
    "V \u00b7 OFFICIAL REPORT",
    "Cause Undetermined",
    "1982 \u00b7 DEPT OF TRANSPORT"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_38.jpg",
   "start": 10154,
   "end": 10482,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test five. The official report. Australian aviation authorities finish a summary after the search, released publicly in nineteen eighty-two.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s38.mp3",
     "dur": 9.84,
     "start": 10164,
     "end": 10460
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_39.jpg",
   "start": 10464,
   "end": 10728,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Its conclusion is short. The reason for the disappearance could not be determined. The pilot is presumed to have died.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s39.mp3",
     "dur": 7.728,
     "start": 10474,
     "end": 10706
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_40.jpg",
   "start": 10710,
   "end": 11128,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The report notes his limited night experience, his unusual route planning, and his stated interest in unidentified objects. It does not say a craft was there, and it does not say there was not.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s40.mp3",
     "dur": 12.864,
     "start": 10720,
     "end": 11106
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 41,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_41.jpg",
   "start": 11110,
   "end": 11407,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "That honest phrase, cause undetermined, is the most important fact in this case. It is not a cover-up, and it is not a confirmation.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s41.mp3",
     "dur": 8.832,
     "start": 11120,
     "end": 11385
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "C",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_42.jpg",
   "start": 11389,
   "end": 11665,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Newspapers did not wait for it. They ran with the strange words from the tape, and the story spread worldwide within days.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s42.mp3",
     "dur": 8.112,
     "start": 11399,
     "end": 11643
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 43,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_43.jpg",
   "start": 11647,
   "end": 11770,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Now we weigh the explanations, one at a time.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s43.mp3",
     "dur": 3.024,
     "start": 11657,
     "end": 11748
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 44,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": [
    "VI \u00b7 THEORY 1",
    "Spatial Disorientation",
    "NO HORIZON \u00b7 INNER EAR \u00b7 LIGHTS"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_44.jpg",
   "start": 11752,
   "end": 12109,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test six. The pilot's explanation. Spatial disorientation. Over open water on a dark night, with no horizon, the inner ear cannot be trusted.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s44.mp3",
     "dur": 10.824,
     "start": 11762,
     "end": 12087
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 45,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_45.jpg",
   "start": 12091,
   "end": 12325,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Pilots call it a black hole effect. The sea and the sky merge, and bright lights can seem to be anywhere.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s45.mp3",
     "dur": 6.72,
     "start": 12101,
     "end": 12303
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 46,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_46.jpg",
   "start": 12307,
   "end": 12727,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Two researchers, Richard Haines and Gregory Norman, studied the recording. They suggested he may have turned inverted without noticing, and mistaken ground or sky lights for another aircraft.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s46.mp3",
     "dur": 12.912,
     "start": 12317,
     "end": 12705
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_47.jpg",
   "start": 12709,
   "end": 13004,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Others noted that bright planets and stars were low in the sky that evening, and can look like moving lights when you are tilted and tired.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s47.mp3",
     "dur": 8.736,
     "start": 12719,
     "end": 12982
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 48,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_48.jpg",
   "start": 12986,
   "end": 13298,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Another idea is rocket debris or a meteor, but that cannot explain a craft that appears to follow a small aircraft for several minutes.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s48.mp3",
     "dur": 9.312,
     "start": 12996,
     "end": 13276
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 49,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_49.jpg",
   "start": 13280,
   "end": 13683,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A rough engine could also be fuel contamination or a mechanical fault, which would add stress to a young pilot. But a mechanical fault does not produce a long metallic shape.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s49.mp3",
     "dur": 12.336,
     "start": 13290,
     "end": 13661
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 50,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_50.jpg",
   "start": 13665,
   "end": 14058,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The disorientation theory explains a lot. It fits his low night experience, and the missing horizon. But it must also explain the green light, and the seventeen seconds of scraping.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s50.mp3",
     "dur": 12.024,
     "start": 13675,
     "end": 14036
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "P",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_51.jpg",
   "start": 14040,
   "end": 14206,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "So we score it as partial. A strong candidate, but not a proven one.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s51.mp3",
     "dur": 4.464,
     "start": 14050,
     "end": 14184
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 52,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "T",
   "ch": [
    "VII \u00b7 THEORY 2",
    "The Visitor",
    "UFO \u00b7 STAGED \u00b7 UNVERIFIED"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_52.jpg",
   "start": 14188,
   "end": 14467,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Test seven. The extraterrestrial explanation. A craft, intelligent, controlled, that played with the plane, then took it away.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s52.mp3",
     "dur": 8.232,
     "start": 14198,
     "end": 14445
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 53,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "U",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_53.jpg",
   "start": 14449,
   "end": 14838,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Researchers have catalogued many reports of unusual lights over Victoria around that time. But a crowd of reports is not a physical craft, and none was ever recovered.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s53.mp3",
     "dur": 11.88,
     "start": 14459,
     "end": 14816
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 54,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "U",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_54.jpg",
   "start": 14820,
   "end": 15092,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Nobody else on the ground or in the air reported the object near him. There is no radar track of it, and no photographs.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s54.mp3",
     "dur": 7.992,
     "start": 14830,
     "end": 15070
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 55,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "U",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_55.jpg",
   "start": 15074,
   "end": 15407,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "And there is another thought, a darker and much more human one: that he chose to disappear. No evidence supports it, and his family always rejected it.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s55.mp3",
     "dur": 10.032,
     "start": 15084,
     "end": 15385
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 56,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "U",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_56.jpg",
   "start": 15389,
   "end": 15735,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "No sign of him was ever reported ashore. No sighting. No contact. The staged disappearance idea, we score as unverified, and unlikely.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s56.mp3",
     "dur": 10.44,
     "start": 15399,
     "end": 15713
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 57,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "D",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_57.jpg",
   "start": 15717,
   "end": 16098,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The alien idea has one real piece of evidence: the words on the tape. But words are testimony, not proof, and a frightened pilot is an unreliable instrument.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s57.mp3",
     "dur": 11.616,
     "start": 15727,
     "end": 16076
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 58,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_58.jpg",
   "start": 16080,
   "end": 16171,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Time to bring the findings together.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s58.mp3",
     "dur": 1.944,
     "start": 16090,
     "end": 16149
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "fx": "sand",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "E",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_59.jpg",
   "start": 16153,
   "end": 16535,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "One more thing before the scorecard. Every report we have comes from one voice on one tape. That is why the transcript, and the seventeen seconds after it, carry so much weight.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s59.mp3",
     "dur": 11.64,
     "start": 16163,
     "end": 16513
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 60,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": [
    "DEBRIEF",
    "The Scorecard",
    "EVIDENCE VS THEORY"
   ],
   "img": "ep/img/shot_60.jpg",
   "start": 16517,
   "end": 16632,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Debrief. Time to score the Valentich case.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s60.mp3",
     "dur": 2.76,
     "start": 16527,
     "end": 16610
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 61,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_61.jpg",
   "start": 16614,
   "end": 17051,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "A real pilot, a real flight, a real recording, a real search: evidence. A report that could not find a cause: evidence. Low night experience and no horizon: real, and relevant.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s61.mp3",
     "dur": 13.488,
     "start": 16624,
     "end": 17029
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 62,
   "fx": "score",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_62.jpg",
   "start": 17033,
   "end": 17436,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Spatial disorientation: partial. A craft with a green light that followed him: no physical evidence. A staged disappearance: no evidence. Alien abduction: unproven.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s62.mp3",
     "dur": 12.336,
     "start": 17043,
     "end": 17414
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 63,
   "fx": "glow",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "V",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_63.jpg",
   "start": 17418,
   "end": 17878,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "The verdict. Unresolved. The most likely story is that a skilled but inexperienced young pilot lost his orientation over a black sea. But that does not explain everything, and nobody should pretend it does.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s63.mp3",
     "dur": 14.256,
     "start": 17428,
     "end": 17856
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 64,
   "fx": "dust",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_64.jpg",
   "start": 17860,
   "end": 18126,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Behind the mystery, there was a young man, with a family who never stopped wondering. Whatever happened out there, they lost a son.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s64.mp3",
     "dur": 7.776,
     "start": 17870,
     "end": 18104
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 65,
   "fx": "stars",
   "motion": "in",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_65.jpg",
   "start": 18108,
   "end": 18463,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "Next case: a place in Africa where nature seems to have switched on a nuclear reactor two billion years before we did. Natural, or ancient technology?",
     "file": "ep/audio/s65.mp3",
     "dur": 10.752,
     "start": 18118,
     "end": 18441
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 66,
   "fx": "none",
   "motion": "out",
   "tag": "",
   "ch": null,
   "img": "ep/img/shot_66.jpg",
   "start": 18445,
   "end": 18743,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "narrator",
     "text": "What do you think happened in those last seventeen seconds? Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.",
     "file": "ep/audio/s66.mp3",
     "dur": 8.856,
     "start": 18455,
     "end": 18721
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}